# Battle City remastered - level 1
#
# One character is one cell, one line is one row. The grid decides the map size:
# every row must be the same length, and this one is 52 x 50 (cols x rows).
# Four cells across and four down make one classic brick block - that is what lets
# a wall crumble by quarters instead of vanishing whole.
#
# 0  empty        4  fortress (the wall around the eagle)
# 1  brick        5  water
# 2  steel        6  bush
# 3  eagle        7  ice
#
# One exception to "one character is one cell": 3 is the eagle's top-left corner and covers 4x4
# cells on its own, so the 15 cells right and below it must be left as 0 - they are its body, not
# free space. Everything else, the fortress ring included, is one character per cell.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored, so feel free to sketch here.
